course: dictionary
lesson: 11081
title: Welwitschia: a strange desert plant
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: A welwitschia is a plant, so it is a noun: the name of a thing. You may never have heard of it, but the sentences around it give you clues. «Welwitschia, a plant of the Namib Desert, has only two leaves its whole life» tells you where it grows and that it is a plant.
explain: Read on for more clues. «They keep growing from the base and the wind tears them into strips.» Keep growing means the leaves never stop getting longer, and tears them means the wind rips them. Try your own meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: Some words are names for a special kind of thing. Nature books call welwitschia a «living fossil». Fossil is an old thing from long ago, and living means still alive, so a living fossil is alive but very old and unusual. A dictionary can confirm what a word means when the clues are not enough.
fact: A welwitschia is a very strange plant from the Namib Desert in south-west Africa, and also from Angola.
fact: «Welwitschia» has only two long, leathery leaves for its whole life.
fact: «Leathery» means tough and smooth, like leather.
fact: Its leaves keep growing from the base and get torn and curled into a messy heap.
fact: Some welwitschias are thought to be well over a thousand years old, so they are called «living fossils».
exercise: Where does welwitschia grow? | On a snowy mountain | In a cold forest in Scotland | In the sea off Australia | *In the deserts of Namibia and Angola
exercise: Copy the word from «the wind tears them into ribbons» that means long thin strips. | *ribbons | desert | fossil | welwitschia
exercise: In nature books welwitschia is called a «living fossil». What does this mean? | A plant made of stone that has died | A plant that grows in water | *A plant that is still alive but very old and unusual
test: How many leaves does a welwitschia have in its whole life? | Five | Ten | One | *Two
test: In science lessons, welwitschia is used as an example of how plants | turn into stone | *adapt to life in the desert | make their own sunlight at night | grow in the sea
exam: Welwitschia appears on the coat of arms of which country? | Angola | Australia | *Namibia | Scotland
